From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:32:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: Decode MPEG-4 Part 2 and H.263 on
 Rockchip VDPU2

VDPU2 decodes an MPEG-4 Simple or Advanced Simple VOP, or an H.263
picture, whole, parsing its video packet and GOB headers itself, with
the registers Rockchip's MPP gives them: the VOL and VOP tools, the
quantiser matrices in raster order, the direct mode TRB/TRD ratios, and
one buffer of the last P-VOP's motion vectors for a B-VOP's direct mode.
It takes the stateless MPEG-4 controls, refusing a VOL with sprites,
data partitioning or reversible VLC, which it has no mode for. The
RK3528's VDPU2 gains it, to 16CIF's 1152 lines, its decoded frames
with it. A VOP without its VOL's time increment resolution is
refused: the decoder parses video packet headers by it, and hangs
without.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
